# Catalyst One — Workspace Layout Architecture (CO-UX-020)

Status: **ENTERPRISE APPROVED** · Priority: **CRITICAL** · Scope: layout architecture

## Philosophy

Every screen belongs to **exactly one** category. Do not mix them.

| Category | Role | Layout bias |
|----------|------|-------------|
| **Registry** | Scan & select | Compact rows · collapsed by default |
| **Workspace** | Execute work | Primary work surface ≈75% · chrome ≈25% |
| **Dashboard** | Analyse | Analytics / KPIs first |

## Registry (e.g. My Deals)

- List-based, not a dashboard of permanently visible KPI cards.
- Default row = compact summary (identity + minimal signals).
- Operational intelligence appears only when the user **expands** a row.
- Users must scan hundreds of Opportunities without scrolling through dashboards.

## Workspace (e.g. Deal Workspace)

- **Kanban-first / execution-first.**
- Executive / identity header provides **context only** (≈25%).
- Lender Pipeline / primary desk occupies ≈75%.
- Do not turn workspace chrome into a second dashboard.

## Nested scroll

Never place vertical scrollbars inside small KPI or registry **cards**.

If detail exceeds the compact surface, open a Right Drawer, Bottom Sheet, or Dedicated page.

Kanban column lanes may scroll as part of the primary work surface (not “cards”).

## Before implementing

Review the change against this philosophy — not only against a checklist of UI fields.
